## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: SpacePresence shows peers in a stable order, the same for any given set of peers, that changes only when the set changes.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [SpacePresence, F-8.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Peers are ordered by hex identity key. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [SpacePresence, F-8.5]
  why: The identity key is the same on every client and does not change while a peer stays, so the order moves only when the set does.
  rejected:
    - Ordering by last-seen time, which every heartbeat refreshes and so reshuffles the avatars each interval.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Presence is keyed by object EID rather than graph path, with a path resolving to its innermost object or to its space.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.4, SpacePresence, PluginState]
  why: The sender holds graph paths and the receivers hold objects; the EID is what both resolve to. Graph paths alone matched neither receiver.
  rejected:
    - Keying by graph path, which the plank header cannot derive from the object it renders.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A viewer expires after two missed heartbeats in both the navtree and plank-header indicators.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.6]
  why: An expiry equal to the broadcast interval let a viewer flicker out between heartbeats, and the avatars applied no expiry at all.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Remove `viewersByIdentity` from the ephemeral state.
  date: 2026-11-03
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [PluginState, F-8.3]
  why: Nothing read it.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: A space's navtree row shows how many peers view the space, as the navbar already does.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.7, SpacePresence]
  why: Space rows render the sync-status glyph, which took no presence, so a space with viewers always showed none.
  rejected: Let the presence surface claim space rows; the navtree renders one end surface per row, so the sync status would be lost.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: When the deck switches workspace, the planks that left `active` are reported as removed.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.3]
  why: The new workspace's layout lists none of the old planks, so peers in the old space kept the viewer until its heartbeat lapsed.
  rejected: Treat an empty heartbeat as clearing the peer; heartbeats are not complete updates, so an empty one cannot be told from a partial one.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Peers get Go to and Jump actions in the app graph; Jump moves the caret and takes focus, as revealing a comment does.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.8, F-8.9]
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Clicking an avatar opens the member list with its row highlighted. The list shows only that object's viewers and ends with a "See everyone in this space" button that opens a People companion in the complementary sidebar listing everyone in the space.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.10, F-8.11, SpacePresence]
```

```mdl
decision D-10: A peer on several devices shows as one row, using the latest device. The navtree presence indicators stay as they are.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.12, F-8.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: Each peer is a hidden graph node under its space, `peer-<identityKey>`, so actions can depend on what the peer views. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.8]
  why: Actions differ per object type and per whether the object is open, so a fixed per-member menu cannot express them.
  rejected: One static action set per member, chosen in the component.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Jump is offered only when the peer's object is open in the deck and its type contributes a `Locator`; Go to only when it is not open. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.8, F-8.9]
  why: Offering both on an open object duplicates one outcome; Go to cannot reveal yet because the target opens after the action returns.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Locations ride the existing `viewing` message, sent with the heartbeat and throttled to one per second on change. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13]
  why: Jump needs only a recent location; the faster rate belongs to following, which raises it only while someone follows.
  rejected: A separate location message; two messages per peer would need their own expiry.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: The companion is named Members, matching the members settings, and links to the members settings to invite more people. In a locked space it shows a placeholder, since there are no other members and no members settings.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-9
  affects: [F-8.10, F-8.11, F-8.14]
```

```mdl
decision D-15: The invite link opens the members settings through `SpaceOperation.OpenMembers` and shows even when no one else is online; the locked placeholder replaces the whole list. Fills in [D-14].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.11, F-8.14]
  why: An empty space is when inviting matters most; a locked space can list no one but you.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: Invite members is a button at the end of the companion's toolbar. Presence rows are built on the react-ui Listbox, so spacing and keyboard navigation come from it, and their actions are visible buttons rather than ghost icons. Notifications comes second in the complementary rail and Members third.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.10, F-8.11]
```

```mdl
decision D-17: The popover opens the companion from a button at the end of its header, and labels its action "Jump"; Notifications and Members take rail positions -2 and -1. Fills in [D-16].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.10, F-8.11]
  why: A full-width footer label overflowed the popover; the header's trailing slot is where a popover's own controls go. Explicit positions keep the rail order from depending on plugin load order.
  rejected: Keep the footer button and widen the popover to fit it.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: Viewers are tracked per session (a tab or app instance), not per identity. A peer with several sessions on an object is one row that expands, behind a disclosure, into a row per session naming its device.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  supersedes: D-10
  affects: [F-8.12, ObjectViewerProps, PluginState]
```

```mdl
decision D-19: Expanded, only the session rows carry actions. Collapsed, the peer's row carries them, acting on the peer's default session.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.12]
```

```mdl
decision D-20: The default session is the one whose anchor (selection or viewport) changed most recently, from typing, scrolling or any other move. A session is active while its anchor changed recently and idle otherwise, shown by a dot alone with no text; editing is not told apart from viewing.
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.12, F-8.15]
```

```mdl
decision D-21: Each running app picks a random session id and sends it, with its device name, in every `viewing` message. The name is the HALO device profile's label, else its platform and OS, matching the devices settings. A message without a session id counts as one session keyed by the identity. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.13, ObjectViewerProps]
  why: A peer cannot read another identity's device profiles, so the sender names its own device. Keying old clients by identity keeps them listed as one session.
  rejected: Look the device up by the gossip envelope's peer id, which only works for one's own devices.
```

```mdl
decision D-22: Receivers derive when a session moved by comparing each message's location with the one before; opening an object or coming back to it counts as a move. Active means moved within the last 60 s. Fills in [D-20].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.15, ObjectViewerProps]
  why: Locations already travel on change, so the receiver sees every move without a new field, and its own clock judges the window, so clock skew between devices does not matter.
  rejected: A sender-side `idleFor` field counting seconds since the last input.
```

```mdl
decision D-23: Each session is a hidden graph node, `session-<sessionId>`, under its peer's node and carries the same Jump and Go to actions for that session. Fills in [D-19].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.8, F-8.12]
  why: Keeps the actions in the app graph, as [D-11] does for peers, so a session's Jump depends on what that session views.
```

```mdl
decision D-24: Sessions on the same device are numbered after its name, the session count sits on a description line under the peer's name, and the caret is the row's trailing Collapsible trigger. The popover takes its 24rem maximum width. The Members companion lists a peer under each object one of their sessions attends, with only those sessions, and its collapsed row acts on the most recently moved of them. Fills in [D-18].
  date: 2026-11-04
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:wittjosiah
  affects: [F-8.10, F-8.11, F-8.12]
  why: Two tabs on one device carry the same name. The count beside the name truncated next to Jump in a 20rem popover. The trailing caret is how Listbox rows collapse elsewhere.
  rejected: A leading caret before the avatar, as first mocked.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap
    literals?: UnionList
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap
    state?: FieldMap
    slots?: FieldMap
    actions?: ActionMap
    emits?: EventMap
    layout?: CodeBlock
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap
    output?: TypeExpr
    errors?: ErrorMap
    effects?: EffectList
    requires?: ServiceList
    note?: Prose
```
